        "app_name": "AED Use Training - ContentsDA",
        "release_date": "1980-01-01T00:00:00.000Z",
        "description": "1. Check for consciousness: Approach the collapsed person and determine if they are conscious.\n2. Establish an airway: If the person is conscious, support their neck and tilt their chin back to establish an airway.\n3. What to do if unconscious: If the person is not breathing, call 911 and describe the situation.\n4. Prepare to use an AED: Locate and move to the nearest AED box.\n5. Apply the AED: Place the AED near the collapsed person and press the power button to activate the machine.\n6. Apply patches: Unbutton the person's shirt and place the AED patches over the right chest and next to the left chest.\n7. Shock: Press the defibrillation button to deliver an electric shock, keeping your distance from the victim.\n8. CPR: Continue CPR after defibrillation, using two hands at a rate of 100 compressions per minute.\n9. Check and repeat: Ends if the patient regains consciousness, but if they don't improve, check their condition and repeat the entire process if necessary.",
